    <h1 class="sp-h1" itemprop="headline">How Fluorescent Fabric Works: The Science of Daytime & Twilight Conspicuity</h1>
    <p class="sp-lede">Fluorescent yellow, pink, and orange appear intensely bright during the day, yet they offer zero safety benefits in the dark. Here is the quantum physics of how these materials convert ultraviolet light into visible brightness, and how to use them safely.</p>
    <p class="sp-research-credit">Based on peer-reviewed research in <em>Human Factors</em> (King et al., 2023) and <em>Transportation Research Part F</em> (Fylan et al., 2020).</p>
  </header>

